WEBVTT

00:00:03.180 --> 00:00:11.980
Intrigue in the Bakumatsu

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:29.840
Tsukikage kooru daichi wo

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:33.670
Korogari fumiwakete yuku

00:00:33.670 --> 00:00:40.880
Horobi to saisei no jidai ga hajimaru

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:44.550
Jiyuu wo omoku kakagete

00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:48.120
Michinaki michi wo erande

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:55.230
Mahiru yori mabushii nichibotsu wo koete

00:00:55.230 --> 00:01:02.230
Yume wo kataru you ni toki no fune wa yuku

00:01:02.230 --> 00:01:11.340
Sono yamiji no mukou ni atarashii yoake

00:01:12.110 --> 00:01:19.250
Bokura wa kitto kurayami no kaina kara umarete kita

00:01:19.250 --> 00:01:22.790
Kanawanu koi wo suruyou ni

00:01:22.790 --> 00:01:26.760
Hikari e to samayotteku

00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:32.000
Doko made mo hateshino nai kono michi wo

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:37.490
Kaeru sube wa nai

00:02:04.530 --> 00:02:08.930
The Enomoto Fleet has departed Edo Bay
and is headed north,

00:02:08.930 --> 00:02:10.900
with the Head of the Conqueror onboard.

00:02:08.930 --> 00:02:10.900
Eighth month, Keio 4

00:02:10.940 --> 00:02:12.470
Edo

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:13.440
Four months ago.

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:15.310
After the bloodless surrender of Edo Castle,

00:02:13.610 --> 00:02:15.240
Nikko

00:02:15.310 --> 00:02:20.110
the flames of the Boshin War have
already spread northward.

00:02:15.340 --> 00:02:20.110
Utsunomiya

00:02:20.680 --> 00:02:25.050
The Shogunate Remnants Army,
led by Keisuke Otori and Toshizo Hijikata,

00:02:25.050 --> 00:02:28.490
seek to escape via Nikko
after the fall of Utsunomiya Castle.

00:02:29.020 --> 00:02:33.330
Nikko Toshogu

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:35.450
Toshogu is considered holy ground,
where Great Lord Ieyasu Tokunaga is enshrined.

00:02:35.560 --> 00:02:42.200
The Shogunate Remnants Army felt that a shrine
should not be exposed to the flames of war

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:46.230
and so, choosing not to go through Nikko,
instead proceeds further north.

00:02:46.370 --> 00:02:51.940
Presently, Kakunojo and Akizuki
travel the Nikko Road,

00:02:51.940 --> 00:02:56.570
pursuing the Head of the Conqueror
headed north with the Enomoto Fleet.

00:03:04.290 --> 00:03:08.590
I guess you weren't aware of your own feelings.

00:03:09.530 --> 00:03:13.260
Well... I have...

00:03:14.030 --> 00:03:16.160
I have something that I want to clarify.

00:03:22.170 --> 00:03:23.470
Oww...

00:03:25.910 --> 00:03:28.380
I'm sorry, my sandal...

00:03:29.750 --> 00:03:30.680
Akizuki-sama?

00:03:32.420 --> 00:03:33.780
Put your foot here.

00:03:35.820 --> 00:03:37.750
I can't do such a thing...

00:03:45.060 --> 00:03:46.430
Don't be silly!

00:03:50.900 --> 00:03:52.670
Hey, look at them.

00:03:53.240 --> 00:03:54.600
It's nice to be young, huh?

00:04:00.710 --> 00:04:02.980
Oh, did your sandal break?

00:04:03.080 --> 00:04:04.580
Y-yes...

00:04:04.580 --> 00:04:06.050
Didn't we have an extra?

00:04:06.050 --> 00:04:06.880
Yeah.

00:04:07.450 --> 00:04:09.220
Um...

00:04:10.120 --> 00:04:11.610
Here, use this one.

00:04:12.260 --> 00:04:13.620
Thank you.

00:04:13.790 --> 00:04:15.090
Don't mention it.

00:04:15.730 --> 00:04:17.920
Thank you. You've been a great help to us.

00:04:18.830 --> 00:04:23.200
We should all help those in need. See you later.

00:04:32.140 --> 00:04:34.200
Akizuki-sama, what is that?

00:04:35.410 --> 00:04:38.810
They likely lost their homes in the war.

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:57.340
The fire that the Shogunate Remnants
set when they abandoned Utsunomiya Castle

00:04:57.340 --> 00:05:03.070
spread all the way to the castle town
and burned down more than 2000 houses.

00:05:03.710 --> 00:05:12.050
There were 300 casualties and 10,000 people
were affected by this Battle of Utsunomiya.

00:05:14.620 --> 00:05:20.320
An Inn in Utsunomiya

00:05:21.360 --> 00:05:23.050
Welcome.

00:05:23.800 --> 00:05:24.930
Can we stay here?

00:05:24.930 --> 00:05:30.040
Yes, but the main part of this inn
was burnt down in the battle the other day,

00:05:30.040 --> 00:05:32.740
so everyone has been sleeping
in the open space.

00:05:32.740 --> 00:05:33.670
That's fine.

00:05:33.940 --> 00:05:36.530
Okay, then you can use the open space.

00:05:37.310 --> 00:05:41.270
You again! Go away!

00:05:41.710 --> 00:05:46.810
Goodness! We get them all the time lately...

00:05:47.290 --> 00:05:52.310
I feel sorry for them, but they never stop
coming around if you show them mercy.

00:05:52.420 --> 00:05:54.690
Oh, Samurai-san over there!

00:05:55.190 --> 00:05:56.690
I knew it was you!

00:05:56.690 --> 00:05:57.680
Over here!

00:05:57.930 --> 00:05:59.360
You're the ones from earlier...

00:06:00.030 --> 00:06:03.900
Just like you said, it's the same guy from earlier.

00:06:03.900 --> 00:06:05.230
Oh, I see.

00:06:05.540 --> 00:06:07.700
What a coincidence.

00:06:14.280 --> 00:06:15.280
Here you go.

00:06:15.280 --> 00:06:16.080
Thanks.

00:06:16.510 --> 00:06:19.450
You two are going to visit
the Great Lord's shrine, too?

00:06:19.450 --> 00:06:21.010
Yes, sort of.

00:06:21.450 --> 00:06:26.320
I was surprised to see this area burnt down.

00:06:26.690 --> 00:06:31.220
Honestly! If they want to fight a war,
go ahead and fight a war!

00:06:31.730 --> 00:06:35.500
But they have no business
getting innocent people involved!

00:06:36.630 --> 00:06:42.110
Now that we're in this new era, I guess the
influence of the Great Lord has deteriorated...

00:06:42.110 --> 00:06:46.570
Hey, you shouldn't say that.
What if an official hears you...

00:06:47.210 --> 00:06:48.650
You're right.

00:06:48.650 --> 00:06:53.520
But it's so depressing around here,
it'll ruin people's visit to the shrine.

00:06:53.520 --> 00:06:55.850
There you go again.

00:06:57.460 --> 00:07:02.520
We might not be the best performers,
but if it helps lifting spirits, it's all right!

00:07:11.900 --> 00:07:14.300
Yo, ha!

00:07:15.070 --> 00:07:20.940
Let me take the liberty of telling you where
I'm from. I'm from Koma Village in Bushu.

00:07:23.210 --> 00:07:26.180
I've been a stray bird since I was 14.

00:07:26.180 --> 00:07:30.280
We've been working nights, hoping
to overcome these troubled times.

00:07:31.360 --> 00:07:35.990
We may sing, but we do no wrong.
Meet the three girls of Shiranami tonight!

00:07:35.990 --> 00:07:38.220
Are you sure you're not old hags
instead of girls?

00:07:38.430 --> 00:07:40.760
We're still young girls at heart!

00:07:46.270 --> 00:07:50.610
Now enjoy our performance!

00:08:06.960 --> 00:08:11.530
From a fancy teahouse...

00:08:11.530 --> 00:08:16.100
Geisha girls are coming...

00:08:16.100 --> 00:08:25.840
Juccho came, running out of the teahouse
and pulled the girl's kimono sleeve

00:08:25.840 --> 00:08:33.520
Geisha girls are running away and
Juccho is chasing them

00:08:33.520 --> 00:08:42.030
Ha, ha, let's run, let's run, let's run!

00:08:42.030 --> 00:08:57.010
Let's run away...

00:08:57.010 --> 00:08:58.500
Way to go!

00:08:59.080 --> 00:09:01.140
Come on, you too!

00:09:01.680 --> 00:09:03.200
What? Me?

00:09:03.410 --> 00:09:07.010
That's right. Don't just sit there.
Come on, help us out.

00:09:07.350 --> 00:09:08.220
Come on!

00:09:08.220 --> 00:09:08.920
But...

00:09:08.920 --> 00:09:09.850
There!

00:09:11.190 --> 00:09:12.120
Here you go.

00:09:18.730 --> 00:09:22.690
Come on, guys! Everyone, dance!

00:09:24.700 --> 00:09:35.080
Even the Sumida River is
close enough to reach with a rod

00:09:35.350 --> 00:09:42.680
So why can't my love reach him

00:09:43.960 --> 00:10:07.770
Let the wind take the dream I just had

00:10:08.080 --> 00:10:17.690
Away to the man I long for

00:10:17.690 --> 00:10:19.210
Here.

00:10:22.830 --> 00:10:24.450
It's good, Big Brother!

00:10:29.570 --> 00:10:35.340
Have you seen Yoshiwara?

00:10:35.340 --> 00:10:40.650
Have you seen the flowers?

00:10:39.910 --> 00:10:40.650
Sir...

00:10:40.650 --> 00:10:48.150
You've seen the flowers, but...

00:10:42.150 --> 00:10:46.450
Which side are you on? The government or...

00:10:47.120 --> 00:10:48.150
Neither.

00:10:48.150 --> 00:10:53.250
I come here often for business,
but you see those kids over there?

00:10:53.360 --> 00:10:56.820
Their parents were killed
in the battle the other day.

00:10:57.500 --> 00:11:00.660
Who knows how they're going to
survive in the future...

00:11:03.700 --> 00:11:08.500
Just kill them all... Kill them all,
the ones fighting this war...

00:11:08.640 --> 00:11:14.480
Come on! What are you doing?
Let's dance! Come on!

00:11:15.710 --> 00:11:20.170
Lord Shoten of Koma enjoys
watching the autumn moon...

00:11:21.150 --> 00:11:25.350
Come on, sir, let's dance together!

00:11:34.400 --> 00:11:38.270
<i>I need you to</i>

00:11:57.420 --> 00:11:59.480
I haven't had such fun in a long time!

00:11:59.990 --> 00:12:02.150
What? That samurai?

00:12:02.490 --> 00:12:06.490
Now that I think about it,
I think I saw him leave a while ago.

00:12:06.760 --> 00:12:07.700
What?

00:12:23.010 --> 00:12:26.040
Don't just sit there.
Come here and keep me company.

00:12:27.490 --> 00:12:30.890
I'm sorry. So you knew I was here...

00:12:31.890 --> 00:12:34.590
I steamed some chestnuts. Here you go.

00:12:34.930 --> 00:12:37.520
Oh, they look very good.

00:12:37.930 --> 00:12:39.690
They must be in season right now.

00:12:39.800 --> 00:12:43.160
Is everything okay with you?
You're out here at a time like this.

00:12:44.640 --> 00:12:46.260
Something tells me that...

00:12:47.770 --> 00:12:50.370
Don't tell me something bad happened to Yojiro!

00:12:52.680 --> 00:12:54.480
Nothing of the sort.

00:12:54.480 --> 00:12:59.280
I told him to run some errands for me.

00:13:23.440 --> 00:13:26.470
He did ask me how to get to the shrine though.

00:13:28.510 --> 00:13:29.880
These must be...

00:13:31.150 --> 00:13:33.740
The three deities that the
inn manager was talking about...

00:13:51.670 --> 00:13:53.000
Is that it?

00:14:51.530 --> 00:14:52.590
Akizuki-sama!

00:15:03.610 --> 00:15:07.480
This is the place where
the Head was once sealed...

00:15:09.750 --> 00:15:16.150
Is that true? Great Lord Ieyasu Tokugawa
was an Eternal Assassin?!

00:15:17.420 --> 00:15:23.190
Then the Siege of Osaka and the Battle of
Sekigahara after that was all to seal the Head?

00:15:24.400 --> 00:15:28.760
Toshogu is a shrine built by the order of Ieyasu.

00:15:30.330 --> 00:15:33.570
Don't tell me they sealed the Head there?!

00:15:34.210 --> 00:15:37.610
But it seems that the seal has been broken.

00:15:38.310 --> 00:15:42.110
Yojiro is there to confirm that for me.

00:15:46.950 --> 00:15:48.380
Moontear Sword?

00:15:48.750 --> 00:15:50.310
Why?

00:16:37.570 --> 00:16:38.760
Akizuki-sama!

00:16:59.720 --> 00:17:00.920
Akizuki-sama!

00:17:04.200 --> 00:17:05.180
Akizuki-sama!

00:17:05.660 --> 00:17:06.490
Stay away!

00:17:08.630 --> 00:17:09.720
Akizuki-sama!

00:17:47.200 --> 00:17:48.870
Where do you think you're going? Go back!

00:18:11.960 --> 00:18:12.760
Leader!

00:18:13.400 --> 00:18:14.390
Behind you!

00:18:21.810 --> 00:18:24.040
Get out of there! Leader!

00:18:29.710 --> 00:18:30.740
Leader?!

00:18:32.580 --> 00:18:33.880
What is this light?

00:18:45.130 --> 00:18:46.460
I can strike them!

00:18:52.140 --> 00:18:53.600
Leader, get out of here!

00:18:58.940 --> 00:18:59.970
Go now!

00:19:02.810 --> 00:19:04.680
This is endless!

00:19:58.600 --> 00:19:59.660
Leader!

00:20:00.240 --> 00:20:01.140
Leader!

00:20:02.070 --> 00:20:03.900
Come on, let's go!

00:20:30.100 --> 00:20:30.930
Jump!

00:20:57.960 --> 00:20:59.660
This sword...

00:21:02.570 --> 00:21:04.300
I was called upon...

00:21:04.300 --> 00:21:06.100
By this sword.

00:21:19.650 --> 00:21:20.620
Akizuki-sama!

00:21:23.990 --> 00:21:26.890
I'm coming with you.

00:21:27.960 --> 00:21:31.160
I'm going to walk the same path...

00:21:42.310 --> 00:21:44.300
I'm coming with you!

00:21:58.390 --> 00:22:02.380
<i>THE</i>
<i>SECRET SWORD</i>
<i>RESONATES</i>

00:22:03.560 --> 00:22:09.330
Sono te wa ai no tsurugi

00:22:09.330 --> 00:22:18.370
Subete no hajimari no akashi

00:22:19.140 --> 00:22:25.100
Hikaru sora no hate

00:22:25.550 --> 00:22:30.320
Yume wa mada maboroshi

00:22:31.460 --> 00:22:34.560
Tsuki no akari kage ouyouni hashiru kono michi

00:22:34.560 --> 00:22:42.070
Tsuki no akari kage ouyouni hashiru kono michi

00:22:42.070 --> 00:22:47.840
Chigireta ai no tsurugi

00:22:47.840 --> 00:23:00.080
Sashidasu saki wa ikusen no namida ga hitotsu ni nari

00:23:00.080 --> 00:23:05.890
Ashita wo kagayakaseru

00:23:05.890 --> 00:23:11.600
Kono te wa ai no tsurugi

00:23:11.600 --> 00:23:20.300
Subete no hajimari no akashi

00:23:33.050 --> 00:23:48.030
EPISODE 16
ACCOMPANIMENT
OF THE FOUR

00:23:33.880 --> 00:23:35.420
Don't you leave your post!

00:23:36.020 --> 00:23:39.860
You may be an ally, but if you leave
your post, I, Hijikata, will kill you!

00:23:39.860 --> 00:23:41.060
Hijikata-san?

00:23:41.260 --> 00:23:43.490
Akizuki... I haven't seen you since Kyoto.

00:23:43.490 --> 00:23:45.400
It has been too long.

00:23:45.400 --> 00:23:47.530
It was the last day of the fifth month in Edo...

00:23:47.730 --> 00:23:51.170
I happened to be there to see
the final moments of Okita-san.

00:23:48.030 --> 00:24:02.570
ACCOMPANIMENT
OF THE FOUR

00:23:51.640 --> 00:23:56.840
This is disturbing, Akizuki. I can see a
negative aura emanating from your body.

00:23:57.140 --> 00:24:01.010
My sword, Izumi no Kami Kanesada,
is telling me so.
